<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    A register a callee only pushes as an alignment pad above a call's stack
    arguments is no argument it reads (option pushpadread on|off, default on),
    while one it forwards AS a stack argument is.

    The XML wrapper only provides the harness architecture; every pass loads an
    in-tree x86-64 ELF through the CLI's own loader and turns the Listing on,
    which is what runs the load-time format-string resolver the probe reads the
    per-call stack-argument counts from.

    pushpad_x86_64 (gcc -O2, show built -Os) is the pad shape: show aligns the
    three stack arguments of __snprintf_chk by first pushing an rdx it never
    set, and run holds an end pointer in rdx at its call to show. Pass 1
    (pushpadread off) reads that pad push as show taking rdx, so the call gains
    a third argument. Pass 2 (the default) reads the format string: the pad
    lies above __snprintf_chk's three stack arguments, so it is no read and the
    call keeps the two arguments show takes.

    pushpadfwd_x86_64 (gcc -O2) is the shape the rule must not break: report
    forwards its third argument as the sixth of printf's variadic arguments
    (its seventh counting the format), pushing it exactly as show
    pushes the pad, and forward forwards its third argument as the ninth of a
    nine-parameter same-binary callee. Pass 3 and 4 (the default) keep both:
    the forwarded register is a real stack argument (below the format count, or
    to a callee whose arity the probe cannot read, so counted as read).
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/pushpad_x86_64</com>
  <com>option listing on</com>
  <com>option pushpadread off</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load function run</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/pushpad_x86_64</com>
  <com>option listing on</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load function run</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/pushpadfwd_x86_64</com>
  <com>option listing on</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load function report</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/pushpadfwd_x86_64</com>
  <com>option listing on</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load function forward</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="PUSHPADREAD #1: off, the pad push reads as an argument the call passes on" min="1" max="1">show\(&amp;v1,cells,a2\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="PUSHPADREAD #2: default, the pad above the format call's arguments is no argument" min="1" max="1">show\(&amp;v2,cells\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="PUSHPADREAD #3: default, an argument forwarded as a format call's stack argument survives" min="1" max="1">logit\(0x2020,a0-&gt;field_0x0,a0-&gt;field_0x8\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="PUSHPADREAD #4: default, an argument forwarded to a same-binary nine-parameter callee survives" min="1" max="1">nine\(v9,v3,v1,v2,v8,v7,v6,v5,v4\);</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
